CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^\[main\.assertion\.\d+\] line \d+ assertion s.b == 0: FAILURE$
--
--
Checks that writes to parts of a variable do not count as overwriting it:
`s` holds the value of the previous iteration at the loop head, so it is not
a loop local and is havoced.
